/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (3. Beliefs, Desires, and Intentions \(BDI\) A common model used in agent-oriented programming \(AOP\) is the BDI model, where agents are characterized by their beliefs \(information about the world\), desires \(goals or objectives\), and intentions \(plans of action\). Example: The chatbot believes the user is seeking customer support, desires to provide the best assistance, and executes a plan to guide the user through relevant troubleshooting steps.)
/E (3. Beliefs, Desires, and Intentions \(BDI\) A common model used in agent-oriented programming \(AOP\) is the BDI model, where agents are characterized by their beliefs \(information about the world\), desires \(goals or objectives\), and intentions \(plans of action\). Example: The chatbot believes the user is seeking customer support, desires to provide the best assistance, and executes a plan to guide the user through relevant troubleshooting steps.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
